program	conformance/K78_singleton_spawn_discard_is_refused.saw
triple	arm64-apple-darwin
twin	same
expect	error
build	refused	`Thread.spawn` hands back a `VoidThread` that must be consumed, and this one is discarded
meets_expect	no: no error contains 'the result of this expression is `Result<std.task.Thread<Void>, std.systemerror.SystemError>` and is silently discarded'
log	"error: `Thread.spawn` hands back a `VoidThread` that must be consumed, and this one is discarded"
log	"  --> examples/conformance/K78_singleton_spawn_discard_is_refused.saw:25:11"
log	"     |"
log	" 25 |     Thread.spawn { work() }"
log	"     |           ^"
log	"   hint: bind it and consume it on every path — `join()` waits for it and takes its result — `Thread.spawn { ... }.join()` is the wait-here spelling — and `detach()` gives the thread to the process. To manage a dynamic set of workers, spawn them into a `TaskGroup` — a group is a declared consumer, so its handles may be dropped freely"
